Every heading Get-SectionBetween's 5 call-sites search for is correctly
cased in the live document today, and CHANGELOG.md carries exactly one
`design-sync-loop`` occurrence at any case -- no mis-cased duplicate for
Get-FirstLineIndex's TEST-037 call to find in error. F-1 and F-2 are
therefore LATENT structural risks in the suite's own dual-runtime parity
(BL-008), not active defects producing a wrong PASS/FAIL on the current
tree.

=== Disposition ===

tests/design-system-contract.tests.{sh,ps1} are explicitly out of scope for
this task to edit (tasks.md T-005 prohibition list; this task's own scope is
tests/run-all.{sh,ps1} plus this verification record). F-1 and F-2 are
reported here, not silently patched -- the same disposition T-001's own
commit applied to the pre-existing DS-010 stale-count defect it surfaced.
Recommended follow-on (not performed by this task): change
Get-SectionBetween's two operators to -cmatch/-cnotmatch (F-1, matches all 5
of its call-sites' actual requirement); give TEST-037's anchor search its
own case-sensitive inline line-search, mirroring how TEST-026 already avoids
routing its case-sensitive `write_files` scan through Get-FirstLineIndex
(F-2), rather than widening Get-FirstLineIndex itself, since 6 of its 7
callers correctly need case-insensitivity.

